              "Despite the tariff fight with the U.S. over the last year, the Chinese manufacturing and export sectors held up well in 2018. Analysts however, attributed the robustness to exporters pushing forward shipment dates — also called front-loading — a phenomenon that was expected to run out of steam, as freight rates indicated",
              "{\"headline\":\"China's December manufacturing activity contracts even more than expected\",\"dateCreated\":\"2018-12-31T01:05:03+0000\",\"datePublished\":\"2018-12-31T01:05:03+0000\",\"dateModified\":\"2018-12-31T05:54:29+0000\",\"author\":[{\"name\":\"Huileng Tan\"}],\"publisher\":{\"name\":\"CNBC\",\"foundingDate\":\"1989-04-17\",\"sameAs\":[\"https://www.facebook.com/cnbc\",\"https://www.instagram.com/cnbc\",\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/cnbc\",\"https://twitter.com/cnbc\",\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CNBC\",\"https://www.youtube.com/cnbc\"]},\"articleSection\":\"China Economy\",\"keywords\":[\"cnbc\",\"Articles\",\"United States\",\"Beijing\",\"Washington DC\",\"Xi Jinping\",\"Donald J. Trump\",\"Politics\",\"World economy\",\"Trade\",\"Business\",\"China\",\"Asia News\",\"Markets\",\"Asia Economy\",\"Business News\",\"World Economy\",\"China Economy\",\"source:tagname:CNBC Asia Source\"],\"video\":{\"description\":\"China's economy is still decelerating, which will impact global trade, warns Frederic Neumann of HSBC.\",\"duration\":\"PT2M45S\",\"name\":\"'We need to see some stabilization in Chinese demand'\",\"uploadDate\":\"2018-12-31T02:22:06+0000\"}}"
